On atlas:

vi /etc/systemd/system/obs-mon.service

sudo systemctl daemon_reload
sudo systemctl enable  obs-mon
sudo systemctl start   obs-mon
sudo systemctl restart obs-mon
sudo systemctl status  obs-mon


=============== obs-mon.service ============
[Unit]
Description=FAST ROACH2 Board Monitor
After=network.target

[Service]
User=obs
Group=obs

WorkingDirectory=/home/obs/observe
ExecStart=/home/obs/venv/observe/bin/python3 /home/obs/observe/obs_monitor.py

# Same proxy-unset as the other services: the server must not route
# web/KATCP traffic through the SOCKS proxy.
Environment="http_proxy="
Environment="https_proxy="
Environment="HTTP_PROXY="
Environment="HTTPS_PROXY="

Restart=always
RestartSec=5

[Install]
WantedBy=multi-user.target
==========================================

Firewall (once):

sudo firewall-cmd --zone=work --add-port=8083/tcp --permanent
sudo firewall-cmd --reload

Notes:
- Port 8083 (scheduler 8080, uploader 8081, controller 8082, monitor 8083).
- Monitor log: ~/log/roach_monitor_YYYYMMDD.log (JSONL, rotates by date).
- The service polls the ROACH2 boards 24/7, including when no browser is
  open; restarting it only loses the in-memory 12 h plot history, never the
  log files.
